    "title": "After 90 years, a central Pa. potato chip company has a new owner - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sue Gleiter ,\n14 hours ago Hartley’s Potato Chip Co., a 90-year-old company rooted in central Pennsylvania, has been sold. Owners Dan Hartley and Kellie Johnson confirmed to the Lewistown Sentinel that they sold the family-operated company to Bill French, owner of Wood-Mode LLC in Kreamer, Snyder County. “As we step into this next chapter,... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 2",
